rner / snake rows / snake columns / diagonal (JPEG-style zigzag - fits the 'zigzag' vocabulary). Invert each read; crib-gated. CyberChef 'Caesar Box Cipher' = column read of a square-ish box. Fixtures single + fragment.\"},\n {\"id\":\"skip-decimation\",\"concept\":\"skip cipher / decimation: ciphertext = every k-th plaintext char mod n\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"c[i] = p[(s + i*k) % n] for gcd(k,n)=1 (dcode 'Skip cipher'); brute k in 2..n-1, s in 0..n-1 with the crib prefix check (n~110 -> ~12k cheap tries; check the first 9 chars before building the rest). Also the non-coprime variant that wraps with +1 per lap. Pun cues: skip, hop, leap, every Nth, stride, step.\"},\n {\"id\":\"redefence\",\"concept\":\"redefence: rail fence whose rails are emitted in a key order (rails permuted), optional offset\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Natural D18 sequel. r<=7 rails: brute r! orders x offsets (7! x 12 too many at full decode: check the crib prefix from the first rail positions only), key also from digits/words in the prompt ('3-1-2', 'THREE'). Reuse rail_rows to get rail lengths, slice the ciphertext in key order, then zigzag-read. Fixtures r=3..5.\"},\n {\"id\":\"transposition-over-strict\",\"concept\":\"a transposition stacked on a seen strict encoding: rail/columnar/reverse of a base64/hex/base32/Morse STRING, or base64/hex of a rail-fenced sentence\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D16-17 stacked two layers; D18 introduced transposition. Cues: base64/hex/b32 alphabet that refuses to decode or has '=' mid-string; Morse/hex that decodes to an anagram of the crib. Add to peel: after a strict decode yields an anagram -> transposition_sweep; before a strict decode that fails -> try rail/columnar/rev on the encoded string (gate: strict decode must then succeed AND read crib). Under the 1 s cap.\"},\n {\"id\":\"word-transposition\",\"concept\":\"word-level transposition: whole words rail-fenced / columnar / shuffled by a key, or each word's letters rail-fenced on their own\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cue: every token is an English word (or an anagram of one), sentence order wrong, slug token intact or anagrammed. Tokens = space-split (16 crib words + slug); apply the transposition_sweep families at token level; per-word mode applies rail/reverse inside each word. Crib-gated.\"},\n {\"id\":\"transposition-plus-letter-map\",\"concept\":\"transposition stacked with a seen letter map (rail fence of ROT13/Atbash/Caesar+7/ROT47 text, either order)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cue: crib multiset test fails, but after rot13/atbash/rot-N/rot47 the multiset matches (letter maps commute with transpositions, so order does not matter for decoding). Run each FREE_CODECS map, re-test the multiset, then transposition_sweep. Fixtures: rail3(rot13), atbash(rail3), rail3(rot47).\"},\n {\"id\":\"riffle-shuffle\",\"concept\":\"perfect riffle shuffle (in/out shuffle repeated k times), odd/even interleave\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'deck'/'shuffle'/'cards' pun. Out-shuffle = interleave halves; in-shuffle starts with the second half; repeat k in 1..order (order of the permutation <= n). Decode = inverse permutation applied k times; crib-gated. Rail 2 offset 0 = one un-shuffle; make sure the sweep reports the right family name.\"},\n {\"id\":\"double-columnar-myszkowski\",\"concept\":\"double columnar transposition and Myszkowski (repeated key letters read together), keys from title/prompt words\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"tgt:columnar covers single keyless widths + one title key. Add: same key twice, two different prompt words, Myszkowski tie rule; keys = every word/number of title+prompt and their uppercase/no-space forms; crib-gated; cap 0.5 s.\"},\n {\"id\":\"bifid-std-square\",\"concept\":\"Bifid / Trifid with a STANDARD (keyless) square, period = full length or 5..10\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Row 75. Fractionation + transposition; keyless when the square is the plain A-Z (I=J) alphabet. Letters only change (spaces/punct kept or dropped), length kept, crib letters not a monoalphabetic map. pycipher Bifid/Delastelle; brute period; crib-gated. Trifid uses a 27-char alphabet (+ '.').\"},\n {\"id\":\"transposition-mastery-joint\",\"concept\":\"short Mastery fragments under a transposition (6-8 chars, key restarts per line)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"D18 line 18 ('p-pr5e6' -> 'pper-56') has no charset cue; decode_chunked missed it and the solver added a slug-gated per-line rail pass. Any future transposition day: register its decoder as a free codec with its day number so _joint_free tries it on each unclaimed line; a 6-char fragment has few distinct rail/columnar reads, so the joined-text slug gate is the only arbiter.\"}\n]\ngaps=new[:6]+[g for g in keep if g['priority']==1]+new[6:9]+[g for g in keep if g['priority']==2]+[new[9]]+[g for g in keep if g['priority']>=3]+[new[10]]\n# move the note gap with p1 up\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if g['priority']==1]+[g for g in gaps if g['priority']==2]+[g for g in gaps if g['priority']>=3]\nids=[g['id'] for g in gaps]; assert len(ids)==len(set(ids))\nassert not set(g['id'] for g in new)&set(k.split(':',1)[1] for k in st if k.startswith('warmups:'))\nfor g in gaps: assert set(g)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'}\npending=[g['id'] for g in gaps if g['action']=='prebuild' and g['id'] not in built]\nprint(len(pending),pending)\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\"\ns=s[:m.start(1)]+body+s[m.end(1):]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\njson.loads(re.search(r\"## Readiness gaps\\n\\n```json\\n(.*?)\\n```\",s,flags=re.S).group(1))\nE\nwc -l reference/coverage/warmups.md; git diff --stat reference/"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"i